    <string name="onboarding_root_title">Rooted phone? Grant everything at once</string>
    <string name="onboarding_root_text">With root, Folark gives itself what normally needs a computer or a trip to Android\'s settings: usage access, its accessibility service (lock gesture), display over other apps (taskbar), adding widgets, the open-apps list for Recents and secure settings. Access to your contacts, calendar, location and phone is not included: each feature asks for its own when you turn it on. It also becomes your home app. Your root manager asks first. You can take any of it back in Android\'s settings</string>
