    <string name="lock_service_label">Folark: screen lock and system actions</string>
    <string name="lock_service_description">Used to lock the screen when you double-tap empty space on the home screen, and for system actions you choose: Android\'s Recents, quick switch and moving the split-screen divider. It never reads screen content. Only if you set per-app taskbar rules or replace Android\'s Recents does it learn which app is in front (its package name). Without \"Display over other apps\" it also shows the Folark taskbar.</string>
